<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>mini_shell</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.11">model.sdf</sdf>

  <author>
    <name>Lucas Wendland</name>
    <email>lwendlan@umd.edu</email>
  </author>

  <description>
    Onshape export of the mini-shell quadrotor. model.sdf is generated from
    model.urdf and must not be hand-edited; model_teleop.sdf is that same
    model plus the multicopter motor and velocity-control plugins.

    After every re-export, check that the composite CoM of base_link plus the
    four props lands on base_link's origin. MulticopterVelocityControl builds
    its rotor allocation from arms measured off the comLink origin rather than
    off the CoM, so an offset there shows up in flight as a fixed tilt and a
    constant drift that nothing trims out. The export currently needs a
    correction in model_teleop.sdf's base_link inertial pose; the lasting fix
    is to move the CAD origin onto the rotor centroid (it sits 7.1 mm forward
    of it in y) and get the mass distribution centred there too.
  </description>
</model>
